{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785947694790,"sessionID":"ses_02d394b98ffeYHOmMJlHD7G5kL","part":{"id":"prt_fd2c7251b0015RcvoxMyPB3aDh","sessionID":"ses_02d394b98ffeYHOmMJlHD7G5kL","messageID":"msg_fd2c718920016hhcWMijyWArtj","type":"tool","callID":"call_00_Lsf6LobGyEiQObZplgH09196","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/02-components/font.md","limit":80},"output":"<file>\n00001| ---\n00002| title: Font Module\n00003| nav_title: Font\n00004| description: Optimizing loading web fonts with the built-in `next/font` loaders.\n00005| ---\n00006| \n00007| {/* The content of this doc is shared between the app and pages router. You can use the `<PagesOnly>Content</PagesOnly>` component to add content that is specific to the Pages Router. Any shared content should not be wrapped in a component. */}\n00008| \n00009| [`next/font`](/docs/app/api-reference/components/font) automatically optimizes your fonts (including custom fonts) and removes external network requests for improved privacy and performance.\n00010| \n00011| It includes **built-in automatic self-hosting** for any font file. This means you can optimally load web fonts with no [layout shift](https://web.dev/articles/cls).\n00012| \n00013| You can also conveniently use all [Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/). CSS and font files are downloaded at build time and self-hosted with the rest of your static assets. **No requests are sent to Google by the browser.**\n00014| \n00015| <AppOnly>\n00016| \n00017| ```tsx filename=\"app/layout.tsx\" switcher\n00018| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00019| \n00020| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00021| const inter = Inter({\n00022|   subsets: ['latin'],\n00023|   display: 'swap',\n00024| })\n00025| \n00026| export default function RootLayout({\n00027|   children,\n00028| }: {\n00029|   children: React.ReactNode\n00030| }) {\n00031|   return (\n00032|     <html lang=\"en\" className={inter.className}>\n00033|       <body>{children}</body>\n00034|     </html>\n00035|   )\n00036| }\n00037| ```\n00038| \n00039| ```jsx filename=\"app/layout.js\" switcher\n00040| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00041| \n00042| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00043| const inter = Inter({\n00044|   subsets: ['latin'],\n00045|   display: 'swap',\n00046| })\n00047| \n00048| export default function RootLayout({ children }) {\n00049|   return (\n00050|     <html lang=\"en\" className={inter.className}>\n00051|       <body>{children}</body>\n00052|     </html>\n00053|   )\n00054| }\n00055| ```\n00056| \n00057| </AppOnly>\n00058| \n00059| <PagesOnly>\n00060| \n00061| To use the font in all your pages, add it to [`_app.js` file](/docs/pages/building-your-application/routing/custom-app) under `/pages` as shown below:\n00062| \n00063| ```jsx filename=\"pages/_app.js\"\n00064| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00065| \n00066| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00067| const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'] })\n00068| \n00069| export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {\n00070|   return (\n00071|     <main className={inter.className}>\n00072|       <Component {...pageProps} />\n00073|     </main>\n00074|   )\n00075| }\n00076| ```\n00077| \n00078| </PagesOnly>\n00079| \n00080| > **🎥 Watch:** Learn more about using `next/font` → [YouTube (6 minutes)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L8_98i_bMMA).\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 80)\n</file>","title":"node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/02-components/font.md","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Font Module\nnav_title: Font\ndescription: Optimizing loading web fonts with the built-in `next/font` loaders.\n---\n\n{/* The content of this doc is shared between the app and pages router. You can use the `<PagesOnly>Content</PagesOnly>` component to add content that is specific to the Pages Router. Any shared content should not be wrapped in a component. */}\n\n[`next/font`](/docs/app/api-reference/components/font) automatically optimizes your fonts (including custom fonts) and removes external network requests for improved privacy and performance.\n\nIt includes **built-in automatic self-hosting** for any font file. This means you can optimally load web fonts with no [layout shift](https://web.dev/articles/cls).\n\nYou can also conveniently use all [Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/). CSS and font files are downloaded at build time and self-hosted with the rest of your static assets. **No requests are sent to Google by the browser.**\n\n<AppOnly>\n\n```tsx filename=\"app/layout.tsx\" switcher\nimport { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n\n// If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight"},"time":{"start":1785947694784,"end":1785947694788}}}}
